22:     back to front by quadrant position: top-left, bottom-right, bottom-left,
23:     then top-right. Later masks overwrite earlier masks where they overlap.
24: 
25:     Key insight
26:     Folding all four quadrants onto the same coordinates gives the output
27:     canvas; the quadrant positions encode the visible layer stack.
28:     """
29:     g = np.asarray(grid, dtype=int)
30:     assert g.ndim == 2, "expected a 2D grid"
31:     height, width = map(int, g.shape)
32:     assert height % 2 == 0 and width % 2 == 0, "input must split into four equal regions"
